    "q-35259": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35259",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{2}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipsoid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of the ellipse with semi-axes $2\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{2},$ centered at $(0,3)$ in the $xz$-plane.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
