    "q-35523": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35523",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{2}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the ellipsoid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(0+1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of the ellipse with semi-axes $2\\sqrt{2}$ and $2,$ centered at $(1,3)$ in the $xy$-plane.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
